<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eskom</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1923">1923</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Electricity Supply Commission</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eskom is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s state-owned electricity utility, founded in 1923 as the Electricity Supply Commission. It generates most of the country's power, largely from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>, and built one of the largest utilities in the world. From 2007 shortages of generating capacity, ageing plants, debt and corruption led to repeated rolling blackouts, known as load-shedding.</p></div>
